Contents
  garnetxlate/    a new crate: an in-process C ABI (cdylib libgarnetxlate.dylib) around the
               translator, so a sandboxed process can turn AIR text into SPIR-V without
               a helper daemon. New files; licence LGPL-3.0-or-later (SPDX headers).
  patches/     our changes to upstream's own files (six upstream-relative changes in
               one diff): raw-buffer byte-offset delivery to called helpers, resource
               path fixes, an "validation skipped" carrier for the in-process path, and
               the workspace member entry. Apply with `git apply` or `patch -p1` on
               top of the upstream commit above.
  COPYING      the LGPL-3.0 text, as shipped by upstream.

How it is used: src/garnet-metal loads Resources/libgarnetxlate.dylib at run time
(src/garnet-metal/rdna4_xlate.h). No LGPL code is compiled or linked into the kext,
the Mesa patches or the MIT-licensed bundle sources; the library is a separate shared
object loaded dynamically. Anyone who builds and distributes libgarnetxlate.dylib must
follow the LGPL for that library (offer its source, including these changes).

No build outputs and no test data derived from Apple software are included. The test
programs in garnetxlate/tests need a corpus directory you generate yourself
(RDNA4X_CORPUS, see tests/corpus.rs); without it they do nothing and pass.
